# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local secrets for real transactional email sending.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (already git-ignored — never commit the
# real values) and fill in the two variables below to enable real order
# confirmation / payment-failure emails sent from fouanjieinstein@gmail.com.
#
# Without these set, checkout still works normally — the order is still
# created — but /api/send-order-email responds 503 and no email is sent.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The Gmail address emails are sent from.
EMAIL_USER=fouanjieinstein@gmail.com

# A Gmail "App Password" for the account above — NOT its normal login
# password. Google requires this for SMTP access from third-party apps.
#
# How to generate one:
#   1. Sign in to the fouanjieinstein@gmail.com Google Account.
#   2. Turn on 2-Step Verification if it isn't already on:
#      https://myaccount.google.com/security
#   3. Go to https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#   4. Create a new App Password (name it e.g. "Meridian Health website"),
#      choosing "Mail" as the app.
#   5. Google shows a 16-character code (spaces don't matter) — paste it
#      below with no quotes.
EMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=

# Restart `npm run dev` after editing this file — Next.js only reads
# .env.local at server startup.
